From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 07:50:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] e2e run: opt-in per-site model judge (--routing DIR) with
 receipts; live-Qwen runbook

--routing DIR gives each site process its own <site_id>.routing.json. The site
builds a Runtime bound to site:<id>, and the shipped verifier judges records
through the judge_record route instead of the lexical judge. An endpoint whose
boundary is not exactly site:<id> is refused; there is no wildcard boundary.
Every model call leaves a receipt (payload, validated reply or error kind,
ledger ref) in the site's own directory, beside the runtime's ledger (model
served, tokens, latency). Without --routing the site config bytes and the run
are the baseline's.

tools/qwen_live/run_live_qwen.sh discovers local OpenAI-compatible servers
(Ollama, llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio) on loopback only, proves one inference and
keeps its request/response, writes the per-site routing files and runs the job.
Seeds other than 0 go through tools/qwen_live/run_seed.py, which bypasses
check_world_counts and is labelled DIAGNOSTIC in the run id.

